{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>From the mouth of infants:</b> R. Moses said: the sense of מפי עוללים is that if they do not speak with their mouths, they themselves will acknowledge Your kindnesses, for You sustain them and multiply them and increase them in body in length and breadth. And what seems right to me: because man is more honored than all created beings below, he said thus. For from the time the child begins to speak—and this is the sense of מפי עוללים—then begins his constitution to receive the power of the wise soul, until it grasps by weighing its knowledge the power of its Creator. For the soul grows stronger day after day, and this is the sense of <b>You founded strength.</b>" "<b>Because of Your enemies:</b> — to nullify the words of those who deny and say: there is no Elohim. And this is the sense of <b>to still enemy and avenger</b>, against those who believe in HaShem whether in speech or in deed."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "Resolved 'א\"ר משה' as 'R. Moses said'; likely referring to R. Moses ibn Ezra or another Moses known to the author."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:39.992607661Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}